page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Preparation03 and original150 — dated status</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:3rem auto;padding:0 1.3rem;color:#172737}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem}td,th{padding:.6rem;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd3de;text-align:left}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.status{padding:1rem;background:#eaf1f7;border-left:4px solid #406b97}a{color:#164e89}</style><h1>Preparation03 launched; original campaign reached 10 terminal records</h1><p class="status"><strong>V4: 0/68 benchmark fits. Original v3.1: 10/150 terminal attempts.</strong> This is a dated evidence snapshot, not a completed comparison or release.</p><p>Packaged '''+esc(status['packaged_at'])+'''. Preparation was observed at '''+esc(P['observed_at'])+'''; the eleventh original attempt was observed at '''+esc(A['observed_at'])+'''. No later state is inferred.</p><h2>V4 preparation</h2><p>The fresh preparation03 controller launched at 06:20:09 UTC on October 16, 2026 after independently audited full14 validation, shifted-cut checks and a successful read-only startup. The startup took 64.926 seconds and left all five owned process identities absent. The live audit verified the actual detached driver, current-host admission, shared lock and CPU 24 public preparation process after the before-check passed. This does not claim a finished prepared-input manifest, fit-time truth isolation, nonlinear fit, or covariance.</p><p>The <a href="../validation04/index.html">fresh full14 validation</a> and <a href="../shifted02/index.html">separate shifted02 diagnostic</a> have their own immutable reports. Earlier failed preparations and the source-profile correction remain separate records.</p><h2>Original v3.1 campaign</h2><p>The ten audited outcomes comprise three failures, five timeouts, one boot interruption and one completion. The ninth attempt exhausted its unchanged two-hour budget. The tenth completed under the original legacy_v3 protocol: its archived result validator accepted all 19 referenced artifacts and 17,280 Cartesian covariance blocks. That legacy classification is not certification of corrected-v3.1 or v4 strict convergence or covariance. The original executables remain unchanged.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Attempt</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Harness seconds</th><th>Exact compact evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table><p>The eleventh frozen QR/legacy-Jacobian request was observed running on CPU 30 at 06:25:57 UTC. This snapshot supplies its exact request and audited ownership observation, not a terminal result. The <a href="../status-preparation-original150-03/index.html">earlier eight-outcome snapshot</a> remains unchanged and is linked rather than duplicated.</p><h2>Evidence and scope</h2><ul><li><a href="status.json">Machine-readable dated status and source identities</a></li><li><a href="manifest.json">Exact package manifest</a></li><li><a href="provenance/preparation03-live-launch-independent-review02.json">Independent preparation launch/ownership audit</a></li><li><a href="provenance/preparation03-actual-startup-independent-review01.json">Independent actual startup audit</a></li><li><a href="provenance/original150-tenth-terminal-independent-review01.json">Independent ten-checkpoint and eleventh-process audit</a></li><li><a href="original150/eleventh-request.json">Exact eleventh request</a></li><li><a href="external-evidence.json">External result artifacts and covariance scope</a></li></ul><p>Raw orbital arrays, 18 of the 19 legacy result artifacts and other bulky scientific inputs stay outside Git. The remaining legacy artifact is the compact preservation receipt included here. The independent scientific audit checked all 19. This publication copied only existing compact records; no bulky scientific artifacts or arrays were rescanned. The <a href="publication-correction.json">publication-only classification correction</a> preserves candidate04 and its independent finding unchanged. A failed first read-only launch-review invocation and its corrected audit remain preserved; they did not change or restart production. No source, physics, priors, weights, thresholds or executable was changed by this publication.</p></html>'''
